From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:38:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wwan: All dialogs of the mobile network as pages with the
 back swipe

Plinius: network mode, network and SIM lock were GtkDialogs, windows of
their own with "Cancel" and "Set" in the window's bar, which
cc-plinius-dialog-pages.c cannot turn into pages. Now they are
AdwDialogs with their own header bar: "Set" (or "Next" for the SIM
lock) at the end, the back arrow and the back swipe instead of
"Cancel". A new dialog is made for every opening, as for the access
points and the modem details, so what show() set up is done once
constructed. The network list takes the rest of the page; the SIM
lock's "Enter current PIN" line wraps, as one line it made the page
wider than the phone.

The modem details were presented for the window, outside the
navigation, and so stayed a dialog; now for the page. The access
points refused to close (can-close false, their own back button steps
from the editor to the list), so they could not be swiped away: on the
list they close with the back swipe now, in the editor the back button
still returns to the list. The panel hears about it through "closed"
too.
